  "notes": "DTP/Def Jam soloist carrying Tim & Bob's 2000s crossover ballad grammar, 2005–2009. The research gives \"62–95 straight; ballads 62–74 half-time\", and the straight band is the base — the two sourced singles sit at 93 and 95 — with `halfTime` false. Three drum deltas quote the duo's kit: \"kick on 1 and the 8th before 3\" at two or three hits a bar with syncopation at 0.2, \"layered clap/snare on 2&4\" with a 1–4 ms offset, and \"16th hats in the hook only\" — a non-continuous lane at 0.2 fill density. The distinguishing fourth is \"tambourine on the backbeat\", a downbeat-placed tambourine with `tambourineMirrorsClap` true. Harmony is \"4-chord m7/maj7 cycles\", so the families run four deep with a 0.16 triad share. The identifying parameter is the counter: \"an obbligato string or guitar line running through — the duo's documented signature from the 'Thong Song' era carried forward\", so `countermelody.densityRatio` is 0.58, well above this section's norm, at +12 with `answer_lick` leading. \"Light high tenor, falsetto hook, close-third stacks\" is the high register and the narrow interval spread. The bass is \"rounded synth bass on roots with a glide into the downbeat\", so a 0.34 `glideProb` and no `bass808` block. ⚠ The research marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with maj7 colour [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
